@startuml candidate-publication-state
title Candidate Publication Gate — proximity-episode:{pair_key} candidate_published

skinparam stateBorderColor #555555
skinparam stateBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam stateArrowColor #333333
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

[*] --> NO_EPISODE

NO_EPISODE --> NEW_EPISODE : confirming ping,\nno existing episode\n(touchProximityEpisode)

NEW_EPISODE --> KNOWN_ASSOCIATE : KNOWN_ASSOCIATE check\n(Neo4j, once per episode)\n-- relationship exists
NEW_EPISODE --> PENDING : KNOWN_ASSOCIATE check\n-- no relationship\n(candidate_published = '0',\nset BEFORE the Kafka publish attempt)

PENDING --> PUBLISHED : Kafka publish\nconfirmed successful\n(candidate_published = '1')
PENDING --> PENDING : later confirming ping,\npublish still not confirmed\n-- retry

KNOWN_ASSOCIATE --> KNOWN_ASSOCIATE : later confirming ping\n-- candidate_published field\nstays absent, never checked again

PUBLISHED --> [*] : TTL gap expires,\nepisode ends
KNOWN_ASSOCIATE --> [*] : TTL gap expires,\nepisode ends

note right of KNOWN_ASSOCIATE
  No dedicated boolean field for this.
  candidate_published is simply never
  written for a known-associate episode --
  its ABSENCE on an existing episode is
  what means "already established as
  known associate," distinct from '0'
  (unscheduled, not yet published).
end note

note right of PENDING
  Written before the Kafka publish is
  even attempted. A crash here leaves
  candidate_published='0' -- indistinguishable
  from "never tried," so the next confirming
  ping retries correctly.
end note

@enduml
